schema_version: s75.script.v1
Top-level keys: schema_version, lineage {split[], merged[]}, scenes[], lyric_sheet {lines[]}, cta {line_id}.
Write the COMPLETE script and lyric sheet for every planned scene. Preserve every scene_id and its sequence, or declare an explicit split/merge lineage. Use only the declared cast_ids; never add an undefined speaker or meaningful extra. Every line carries line_id, character_id, exact text, start_s, end_s and delivery (spoken|sung). The first 12 seconds carry spoken/articulated words. Each scene after the first must name its causal_predecessor (the previous scene_id or its causal_outcome_id) and a causal_outcome_id that makes the next scene necessary. Mark exactly ONE scene with solution_introduced=true, and it must come after the consequential choice and emotional turn. Mark every later scene where behavior visibly changes with behavior_change=true. Exactly one CTA line, marked role="cta", after the earned outcome. Return lyric_sheet.lines repeating every sung line identically (line_id, character_id, text) so the song cannot bind to another draft. Reply with JSON only, no prose and no code fence.
